      })
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Think of AI models like talented but unreliable interns. They're smart, fast, and can handle many tasks, but you can't just give them work and walk away. You need to provide clear instructions (prompts), check their work (evaluation), give them the right resources (context/RAG), handle situations where they're confused (error handling), and supervise their outputs (guardrails). You wouldn't let an intern send emails to customers without review; don't let your AI do it either. This analogy helps explain why AI engineering exists-the models are powerful but need thoughtful integration and oversight."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
