      })
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Remember the difference between closed-book and open-book exams? A closed-book exam (pure LLM) tests what you memorized; an open-book exam (RAG) lets you reference materials to find answers. RAG systems give the AI \"textbooks\" to consult, making it more accurate and reducing hallucinations. The AI's job shifts from \"know everything\" to \"know how to find and synthesize information\"-much like how students perform better when they can reference materials. This explains why RAG is so powerful: you're not asking the model to memorize your entire knowledge base; you're giving it the ability to look things up."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
